   "columns": [
    [
     {
      "type": "textmedia",
      "header": "<h1> FAQ </h1>",
      "body": "<p class=\"large-text\">Frequently asked questions</p>",
      "images": [],
      "videos": [],
      "pos": "text",
      "cols": 1,
      "valign": "top",
      "ftype": "text",
      "id": "c3794",
      "bg": "",
      "space": {
       "before": "default",
       "after": "default"
      }
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "type": "accordion",
      "header": "",
      "items": [
       {
        "title": "What is webTMS?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>ZOLLER webTMS Tool Management Solutions is the web version of the desktop application TMS, which can be used on various devices. As webTMS has been developed from scratch, not all modules and functions of the TMS desktop version are currently available.</p> <p>Advantages of a web application: No installation on devices required. Any device with a browser (PC, smartphone, tablet, notebook, etc.) can access webTMS immediately. Installation, configuration and maintenance only take place on the host device, which significantly reduces the administrative effort.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c3791",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "What is the webTMS StartUp Edition?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The webTMS StartUp Edition is the first version of webTMS to be launched on the market. It is pre-installed on all setting and measuring devices as well as TMS hardware products»(keeper«, »autolock«, »toolOrganizer«, »zTower«, »toolStation«, »cockpit«) so that customers can get started immediately.</p> <p>As soon as the device is connected to the network, simply start webTMS. From this point on, the software can be used on any device with a browser without any additional installation.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c3915",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Can the webTMS StartUp Edition also be used by TMS customers?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>This version of webTMS is not compatible with TMS as it is hosted on the IPC of the presetting and measuring machine or a TMS hardware product that is not designed for this dual use. The simultaneous use of both systems can lead to performance problems and crashes.</p> <p>A compatible on-premise version (BETA phase), which is installed and hosted on a customer's server, is currently under development.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c3917",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "How do I install or set up webTMS?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>No installation is required as webTMS is already pre-installed on the setting and measuring device or a TMS hardware product. All you need to do is create a test license (or select a purchased license) and start webTMS on the device that is to act as the host. Optionally, the database, graphics and document path can be configured.</p> <p>To enable access from other devices, the setting and measuring device or a TMS hardware product must be integrated into the network. Access is via the standard ports 80 and 443.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c3921",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "How can a customer purchase or extend a license?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Currently, customers can contact their ZOLLER contact person to request an individual offer. The license is sent manually by the software provisioning team, but this process will be automated in the future. In future, customers will be able to use MYZOLLER for this. Customers can choose between monthly, semi-annual or annual billing with a minimum term of one year.</p> <p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"/en_DE/company/contact\">Contact us now</a></p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c3919",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      "ftype": "accordion",
